    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive outlook for the Austin Waves centers on the elite profile of **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the board with a score of 82.40. Facing Cavalli, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a favorable matchup against a 4.06 xERA arm and a significant platoon edge, making him our primary engine for runs and power. Complementing this, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Heliot Ramos** (66.96) serve as high-ceiling pivots. **Heliot Ramos** is particularly intriguing; despite the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, his elite park factor and matchup against Severino\u2019s 4.63 xERA provide a substantial boost, keeping him well above our \"Strong\" start threshold.\n\nThe primary tension in today\u2019s optimization involved **Nolan Schanuel** and **Coby Mayo**, who remain on the bench with scores of 48.38 and 44.92, respectively. **Nolan Schanuel** was the closest to cracking the lineup, but his struggles against the 3.52 xERA of Wrobleski and the resulting SP skill penalty relegated him to the pine. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** earns the nod over these options\u2014despite the 4% penalty for facing a high-hold pitcher like Bassitt\u2014due to his high-utility role and his elite sprint speed profile, which we continue to overweight given the scarcity of stolen bases in this format.\n\nManagers should monitor the status of **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Heliot Ramos**, all of whom are currently listed with pending lineups. While we have modeled them as middle-to-bottom order hitters, any shift into the top three of the order would drive their scores even higher. Conversely, proceed with caution regarding **Jackson Merrill**; despite his talent, his matchup against the 2.98 xERA of Gilbert creates a significant volatility risk, reflected in his marginal 52.65 score. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving our current outfield depth to carry the load as we look to capitalize on these specific platoon alignments.",
